# Line-ending policy for Orkestr.
#
# WHY: this repo is developed on Windows, where Git's core.autocrlf setting is
# per-machine. Without a committed policy, a contributor whose machine lacks
# core.autocrlf=true reintroduces CRLF into the index and every subsequent diff
# shows thousands of phantom line changes, burying real review. Pinning the
# policy in-repo makes it machine-independent.
#
# The index is already fully LF, so adding this file changes no stored content.

# Text files: detect automatically, always store LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native shells expect CRLF on disk.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.db   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated lockfile: tracked, but not worth reading in a diff.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated=true
